77:segments that show significant differences, BUAN reports higher MD and DNT also reports higher MD anomaly scores in both MCI and AD groups when compared to CN. In Figure 4, we plot the along-tract -log 10 ( p FDR ) values from AD vs. CN comparisons in the commissural tracts (CC mid, forceps major and forceps minor ). DNT reveals MD abnormality patterns similar to BUAN along the length of the tracts, even when accounting for shape changes.
